<title>UK: FTA survey expects growth in UK air freight trade.</title>
<headline>FTA survey expects growth in UK air freight trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of British imports and exports carried by air freight is expected to increase in the next quarter, the Freight Transport Association's (FTA) transport activity survey for April 1997 shows.</p>
<p>The net opinion on all routes was for an increase in air freight for all import and export routes with no respondents volume expecting less volume on any import routes.</p>
<p>Details of the FTA survey showing expectations of change in air freight volume by percentage of total responses include:</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p> Trade Routes     More     Same    Less</p>
<p> North America    35	 65	 0</p>
<p> South America    13	 80	 7</p>
<p> Australasia	25	 69	 6</p>
<p> Southern Africa  14	 79	 7</p>
<p> Far East	   50	 50	 0</p>
<p> Middle East	36	 57	 7</p>
<p>(Inc Japan)</p>
<p> Western Europe   31	 69	 0</p>
<p>IMPORTS</p>
<p> Trade Routes     More     Same    Less</p>
<p> North America    43	 57	 0</p>
<p> South America    18	 82	 0</p>
<p> Australasia	27	 73	 0</p>
<p> Southern Africa  27	 73	 0</p>
<p> Far East	   38	 62	 0</p>
<p> Middle East	30	 70	 0</p>
<p>(Inc Japan)</p>
<p> Western Europe   38	 62	 0</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
